Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight One-Shot Activation Ceremony P0 Design

@ [design_uuid] 32f07e8c-a7d0-4645-9ad5-836baf4b8145
@ [source_uuid] f0ff26c7-eb2a-43c2-95ee-00ceee790387
@ [canonical_uuid] d2724a39-56bd-47ae-8787-064a6196dbfb
@ [predecessor_bookend] 0674395c78a998ce1c36c714e52bae68d0f83f58

& [Architecture]
  + a pure ceremony compiler owns proposal and transition correspondence while a separate verifier replays raw forms
  + external operator decision acquisition remains outside the compiler and is admitted only through an exact signed decision form
  + a future private bridge may translate one admitted authorization into the runner's private affine permit
  + permit consumption occurs before control enters the existing runner so every attempted process path spends the sole capability
  + runner output crosses back as one sealed receipt and must pass an independent verifier before terminal completion

& [StateMachine]
  + proposed to proposal_verified to decision_supplied to decision_admitted to permit_minted to permit_consumed to receipt_verified to terminal_closed
  + admitted_reject closes at decision_admitted without a permit
  + any refusal closes immediately; any failure after permit consumption closes abandoned_after_consumption
  + no state has an edge to an earlier state and no terminal state has an outgoing edge

& [AuthorityConservation]
  + proposal and verification carry zero contact authority
  + operator authorize contributes exactly one finite decision authority
  + mint exchanges that authority for one private permit without multiplying it
  + consume exchanges the permit for one attempted runner entry
  + receipt and closure describe results and cannot recreate decision permit or retry authority

& [ImplementationSequence]
  + publish this formation and immediate bookend
  + implement pure forms compiler verifier fixtures and static absence gates provider-free
  + publish pure implementation and immediate bookend
  + separately source-govern the private mint-and-consume bridge and live initiation route

& [NonAuthority]
  + this design performs and authorizes no permit mint process spawn OpenSSH contact EVO-X2 observation provider request remote call or effect
